 {"url":"index.html","id":"wiki","line":16,"endLine":21,"kind":"heading","label":"Wiki","title":"","text":"Knowledge space for stuff I study.\nMathematics: notes on ideas, and the books they came from."},
 {"url":"index.html","id":"search","line":22,"endLine":25,"kind":"heading","label":"Search","title":"","text":""},
 {"url":"math/books/chrystal-algebra.html","id":"","line":2,"endLine":26,"kind":"page","label":"Chrystal, Algebra: An Elementary Text-Book","title":"","text":"A book"},
 {"url":"math/books/chrystal-algebra.html","id":"chrystal","line":18,"endLine":26,"kind":"heading","label":"Chrystal, Algebra: An Elementary Text-Book","title":"","text":"G. Chrystal, Algebra: An Elementary Text-Book for the Higher Classes of Secondary Schools and for Colleges, Part I. First published in 1886. The book is in the public domain: the author died in 1911.\nRe-typeset PDF, from David Moews' library: https://djm.cc/library/Algebra_Elementary_Text-Book_Part_I_Chrystal_edited.pdf\nScan on the Internet Archive: https://archive.org/details/algebraelementar01chryuoft\nRead so far: chapters I to IV of Part I, the fundamental laws, monomials and indices, the theory of quotients, and the distribution of products. The book gives final answers to its exercises but no derivations."},
 {"url":"math/books/hammack-book-of-proof.html","id":"","line":2,"endLine":26,"kind":"page","label":"Hammack, Book of Proof","title":"","text":"A book"},
 {"url":"math/books/hammack-book-of-proof.html","id":"hammack","line":18,"endLine":26,"kind":"heading","label":"Hammack, Book of Proof","title":"","text":"Richard Hammack, Book of Proof, edition 2.2. An introduction to writing proofs: sets, logic and counting first, then the kinds of proof, then relations, functions and cardinality. The book is © Richard Hammack and released under the Creative Commons Attribution-No Derivative Works 3.0 License.\nThe author's page: https://www.people.vcu.edu/~rhammack/BookOfProof/\nMirror: https://richardhammack.github.io/BookOfProof/\nRead: all thirteen chapters. The book prints solutions to its odd-numbered exercises."},
 {"url":"math/books/hobson-plane-trigonometry.html","id":"","line":2,"endLine":25,"kind":"page","label":"Hobson, A Treatise on Plane Trigonometry","title":"","text":"A book"},
 {"url":"math/books/hobson-plane-trigonometry.html","id":"hobson","line":18,"endLine":25,"kind":"heading","label":"Hobson, A Treatise on Plane Trigonometry","title":"","text":"E. W. Hobson, A Treatise on Plane Trigonometry, seventh edition, Cambridge University Press, 1928; first published in 1891. The book is in the public domain: the author died in 1933.\nScan on the Internet Archive: https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.85807\nNot started. The book gives no answers to its examples."},
 {"url":"math/index.html","id":"mathematics","line":15,"endLine":18,"kind":"heading","label":"Mathematics","title":"","text":"Notes on what I study, written once the idea has settled: one idea per page, in my own words, and a page for each book I work through."},
